From 37f265e038ef3d248edc82787bd756265d2f63ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Launchers for coordinate-fusion DAgger (E1 GT, E2 LLM) and
 flag-safe eval

run_dagger_coord_fusion.sh {gt|llm}: plain try5 DAgger (no teacher, no
refiner) with MODEL.MAP_ENCODER.coordinate_fusion, the release try5 DAgger
schedule (30000 iters, decay 2000, warmup 500), elevation axis y and map
modules from init.
  gt  (E1): gt.online121c369 maps, start_position in cells (0.5),
            SS-ETP-PriorGT / PriorGTTry5Policy from try-5-r1p5_step_387500;
            reference the dz GT teacher (73.84).
  llm (E2): LLM-Grid maps (1.0), SS-ETP-LLM / LLMGridTry5Policy from
            model_step_460000; reference historical try5 (65.09).
COORD=False runs the same arm without coordinate fusion in its own
directory. Auto-resume as in the other launchers.

Coordinate fusion adds no weights, so a checkpoint evaluated with the wrong
flag would run without error and give wrong numbers. Two guards:
  * the launcher writes eval_args.txt (the arm's model/map options) into the
    run directory; eval_run.sh (and so eval_iters.sh) appends it, and
    eval_raster_donor.sh appends the one next to CKPT_PATH except the LLM
    cache key it replaces;
  * the PriorGT trainer compares coordinate_fusion in the checkpoint's saved
    config with the current one when loading and refuses a mismatch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CAaWoeW35zu5bncqujUPPQ
